within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.A_AlimentaryTractAndMetabolism.A08A_AntiobesityPreparationsExclDietProducts.A08AA02_Fenfluramine;
model Fenfluramine_Sheeni2025_PD_mes_4
  "sigmoid_emax exposure-response sweep — Sheeni_2025 :: MES (seizure protection)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 0,      // [1; % × 0.01]
    Emax = 1,  // [1; % × 0.01]
    EC50 = 3.4e-05,  // [kg/m3; ng/mL × 1e-06]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 ng/mL per second
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 340, Interval = 0.68),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Fenfluramine_Sheeni2025_PD_mes_4</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Sheeni Y et al., <i>Epilepsia 66(11):4501–4512</i> 2025 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/epi.18542\">doi:10.1111/epi.18542</a>) — seizure protection [%] against d-norfenfluramine ng/mL — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: sigmoid_emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =          0 %        drug-free response (baseline) (Bottom, Q324)
  Emax  =        100 %        maximal effect term (Top, Q320)
  EC50  =         34 ng/mL    exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC50, Q321)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ng/mL of d-norfenfluramine per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 0   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (34 ng/mL)  response 0.5
  exposure -> infinity  response 1</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Sheeni_2025: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Fenfluramine_Sheeni2025_PD_mes_4;
